                <pb facs="0789" n="679" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg679"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/3179: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Forbes</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-12-12T15:00:00-05:00">December 12, 1931—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>264. Your 259, December 12, 8 p.m. In my opinion, you should talk over this
                    matter at once with Baron Shidehara unless you feel it is not advisable to take
                    up the matter except with Shidehara’s successor.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
